# Fast post-build smoke suite in the validation class for the reduced sizing profile, executed
# through two drivers. The psql test creates a table and a covered index and loads it in prepare,
# then runs fixed point, range, and write statements in run so that its row counts are
# deterministic. The java-main test runs a single Phoenix client class on client 0, verifying the
# class path, client configuration, and JVM options of the client role by invoking SchemaTool to
# extract the DDL of a user table created from the same schema file during the test's prepare
# phase. Because SchemaTool establishes its own connection rather than reading px.jdbc.url, its
# request metrics remain disabled. Every test leaves the cluster as it found it, with each test
# dropping its tables during the restore phase.

suite: smoke
description: The smoke check of a build, through the psql and java-main drivers
class: validation
timeout: 600

test: sql
  name: Create, load, index and query one table
  driver: psql
  args: --prepare sql/smoke-schema.sql sql/smoke-query.sql

test: client
  name: Extract the DDL of a user table with a Phoenix client class
  needs: sql
  driver: java-main
  args: --prepare sql/smoke-schema.sql
  args: org.apache.phoenix.schema.tool.SchemaTool -m EXTRACT -tb ITEMS -s PX_SMOKE
